 Run hardware-free tests with `python -m pytest tests`. Neither API nor tests
 starts a server or sends motor commands.
+
+## Weld seam profile API
+
+```python
+from weldfinder import find_weld_seam, SeamSettings
+
+# Existing calibrated native cloud only; no camera or worker is created.
+seam = find_weld_seam(cloud, settings=SeamSettings(torch_standoff_mm=150.),
+                      previous_point_mm=None)
+if seam['status'] == 'found':
+    point_camera_mm = seam['seam_point_mm']
+    camera_from_torch = seam['camera_from_torch']
+```
+
+Input is `PointCloud` or its native `to_dict()` payload (`xyz_mm`, aligned native
+`uv`, camera frame, mm). Original points are never changed; resampling only locates
+features. Spacing-weighted native measurements determine the valley depression
+centroid. A height step uses the midpoint of its two fitted observed limits. A
+robust quadratic trend removes smooth background curvature before sharp valleys
+and supported height steps are tested. A broad inside corner is separately
+recognized from two long fitted 3D lines: it must improve sharply on smooth
+quadratic curvature, have a substantial tangent discontinuity, and have an
+intersection supported by two adjacent qualified flanks. A small occluded root
+can be inferred only from those non-collinear lines within 1.5 mm of an observed
+return; `inferred_root=True` and `centroid_method=supported_flank_intersection`
+explicitly label this estimate. No returns are synthesized. Flat missing intervals
+never qualify. Two adjacent fitted flanks must meet span
+and residual gates. Omitted native scan coordinates never establish a fabricated step or evidence
+that the seam disappeared. Found features require actual flank support or the
+explicit bounded inside-corner intersection described above. UV scan-coordinate
+gap defaults to at most 3 pixels; configure it explicitly for intentional sampling.
+
+The JSON result includes `status` (`found`, `no_seam`, `invalid`, `ambiguous`),
+`found`, `units='mm'`, `coordinate_frame='camera'`, `quality`, `settings`, detached
+native `provenance`, and nullable geometry. Only `no_seam` means a usable contiguous
+profile without a supported sharp feature. Insufficient/rough/missing stripe,
+poor flank support and ambiguity must not end a robot seam search. Competing
+features return `ambiguous`; an optional measured prior in current camera mm
+selects only within `association_radius_mm` (default 4 mm), without silently
+switching surfaces. Freshness, matching calibration/session identities and measured
+robot-pose registration remain the consumer's responsibility.
+
+Found geometry is `seam_point_mm`, `flank_lines_mm` (2 x 2 x 3 endpoints),
+`stripe_direction_camera`, `surface_normal_camera` (outward toward camera),
+`scan_direction_camera` (perpendicular to stripe on the surface), and
+`camera_from_torch` (4 x 4 rigid transform; translation in mm). Torch +Z points
+toward the measured seam along the two-flank normal bisector, +X follows the
+transverse stripe, +Y is the scan direction. Its origin is the measured centroid
+plus outward normal times `torch_standoff_mm` (default 150 mm). Thus it is centered
+between the two observed flanks, at a 150 mm sensing/replay clearance. An eventual
+contact welding offset requires an explicitly qualified installed torch transform;
+this API neither actuates welding nor redefines a robot TCP. The robot service
+owns bidirectional motion, minimum search extent, endpoint confirmation, path
+assembly, registration, persistence and replay. Panels display those results.
+
+Default geometric detection is exploratory, not dimensional or welding-process
+qualification. Features wider than the configured width (8 mm), unobservable
+occluded roots, very narrow/small grooves and unsupported complex profiles may be
+unresolved. The centroid is a profile depression centroid, not a guaranteed hidden
+joint root. Inspect `feature_kind`, `prominence_mm`, `width_mm`, `flank_rms_mm`,
+`centroid_method`, and `accuracy_qualified=False` in quality. No surface rescaling,
+calibration update or nominal geometry substitution occurs.
+
+
+A native jump across an inside corner can activate both the step and corner
+algorithms. Only when both pairs of fitted flank lines agree geometrically,
+including their angle and distance to the same root within residual-derived
+bounds, does the API retain the inside-corner intersection as a single physical
+feature. This does not merge features merely because their points are close or
+a prior prefers one. `quality.raw_candidate_count`, `candidate_count`, and
+`duplicate_candidates` retain the discarded step midpoint, retained corner root,
+and both measured flank-equivalence checks and bounds. Independently supported
+distinct features remain ambiguous, including two within the association radius.
+When a prior is supplied, `association_prior_camera_mm` and
+`candidate_prior_distances_mm` preserve the exact camera-frame association input
+and distances for later diagnosis. No nearest-feature shortcut is applied.
